{
 "_doc": "Tabard equipment. Every item says which LAYERS it uses: paint = the outfit painting whose boxes it paints for its slot (data/outfits.json id; the boxes come from data/regions.json slots); geosets = swap-in mesh pieces it turns on; hides = pieces it forces off (a robe hides boot cuffs); attach = a separate model on a bone (data/props.json id). js/tabard.js reads this file only. Names are what a player sees. hair: a head item's rule for the hair layer (js/hair.js) — 'hide' (no hair shows: closed helms, hoods), 'under' (the hair's tucked version: crown pressed under the hat, buns/spikes dropped, hair below the rim kept), 'keep' (untouched), or one per body { male, female }; the old hidesHair: true still means 'hide'. hairStyle: a Hair-slot item that just picks a hair style (data/hair.json id) in the look's colour. fal: a fal.ai weapon or shield (avatar-3d/fal/data/catalog.json id) held on the Tabard grips; every held fal item is also offered automatically as 'fal:<id>' (js/tabard.js loadTabardData), so new fal weapons need no entry here. attach may be a list of props (the full tabard: chest panels + belt flaps). only: the named parts of a prop to wear (tabard flaps: 'front', 'back'). hold: 'pole' = a staff, spear or two-hander: held on the pole grip (shaft through the fist at a right angle to the forearm) with the elbow bent forward in idle/walk so it stands up; long fal weapons get it by themselves. shrinkAbove: {k, from} = the part of a weapon more than `from` metres above the fist is shrunk by k (shaft + head), the handle in the fist keeps its size. turn: degrees a held item is turned about its own long axis (the bow: string toward the archer). An entry keyed 'fal:<id>' keeps the automatic id (games map to it) while adding options (shrinkAbove on the oversized clubs).",
